  ($j$qeelasee-bottom-volume-lashes$j$, $j$Bottom lash extensions in short 5mm, 6mm and 7mm lengths, made for the lower lash line. Add a few to the bottom lashes to balance a dramatic top set, open up the eye or create the doll-eye and anime looks many clients now ask for. Choose a thickness from 0.05mm to 0.20mm in J, B or C curl.$j$, $j$["Short 5, 6 and 7mm lengths", "For lower lash line extensions", "0.05-0.20mm thickness", "J, B and C curls"]$j$::jsonb, $j${"title": "Bottom Lash Extensions 5-7mm for Lower Lashes | Kenya", "meta": "Short 5, 6 and 7mm lashes for lower lash extensions, in 0.05-0.20mm and J, B or C curl. Finish full sets with a soft bottom line. Order in Kenya.", "keyword": "bottom lash extensions", "keywords": ["lower lash extensions", "bottom lashes Kenya", "under eye lash extensions", "5mm lashes", "short lash extensions"], "alt": "Bottom lash extensions tray of short 5-7mm black lashes with an eye wearing lower lash extensions", "sections": [{"heading": "How artists use bottom lashes", "body": "Lower lashes are short and fine, so they need short, light extensions. Use the 0.05mm or 0.07mm lashes in J or B curl for a soft natural bottom line, or 0.10mm and up for a defined, graphic lower lash."}, {"heading": "Working on the lower lashes", "body": "Ask the client to look up, secure the lower lashes away from the upper lashes with tape, and keep the glue dot tiny. Lower lashes shed faster, so tell clients bottom extensions usually need refilling sooner than the top set."}, {"heading": "Ordering from Lashtribe Africa", "body": "Lashtribe Africa is a preorder wholesale shop for lash technicians in Kenya. Your order joins the next supplier shipping batch, which leaves around the middle and the end of every month, so you pay close to source prices instead of local shelf prices.\n\nBuy the minimum quantity shown on this page to get the wholesale price; smaller orders pay the retail price. Pay by M-Pesa or card. Shipping to our office is worked out by weight at checkout, and we contact you as soon as your batch lands to arrange delivery to your salon."}], "specs": [{"label": "Type", "value": "Lower (bottom) lash extensions"}, {"label": "Thickness", "value": "0.05mm, 0.07mm, 0.10mm, 0.15mm, 0.20mm"}, {"label": "Curl", "value": "J, B, C"}, {"label": "Length", "value": "5mm to 7mm single lengths"}, {"label": "Fibre", "value": "PBT synthetic fibre from Korea"}, {"label": "Colour", "value": "Black"}, {"label": "Lengths per tray", "value": "Single length"}], "faqs": [{"q": "Where can I buy bottom lash extensions in Kenya?", "a": "Order bottom lash extensions here on Lashtribe Africa. Add it to your cart, pay by M-Pesa or card, and it ships with the next supplier batch to our office in Kenya. We contact you when it arrives to arrange delivery to your salon or home."}, {"q": "How much are bottom lashes in Kenya?", "a": "The price on this page is the live price. Order the minimum quantity for the wholesale price; smaller orders pay the retail price. Shipping is added by weight at checkout, so you see the full cost before you pay."}, {"q": "Can you put extensions on bottom lashes?", "a": "Yes. Use short, light lashes like these and a very small amount of glue. Lower lash extensions usually do not last as long as top lashes."}, {"q": "Which curl is best for lower lashes?", "a": "J or B curl for a natural look; C curl for a more open, doll-like look."}]}$j$::jsonb, $j$Bottom lash extensions tray of short 5-7mm black lashes with an eye wearing lower lash extensions$j$),
  ($j$qeelasee-brown-lash$j$, $j$Brown lash extensions give a softer, more natural finish than jet black. They suit clients with light or brown natural lashes, blonde or red hair, or anyone who wants a no-makeup look. This tray comes in 0.05mm and 0.07mm for volume and hybrid work and 0.10mm for classic sets, in C or D curl.$j$, $j$["Soft brown colour", "0.05, 0.07 and 0.10mm", "C and D curl", "8-15mm single lengths or mixed tray"]$j$::jsonb, $j${"title": "Brown Lash Extensions 0.05-0.10mm Trays | Kenya", "meta": "Brown lash extension trays in 0.05, 0.07 and 0.10mm, C and D curl, 8-15mm. A softer, natural look than black. Order wholesale in Kenya.", "keyword": "brown lash extensions", "keywords": ["brown eyelash extensions Kenya", "brown volume lashes", "natural brown lashes", "brown lash tray", "light skin lash extensions"], "alt": "Brown lash extensions tray with rows of brown lashes and a close-up of the brown fibres", "sections": [{"heading": "Who it suits", "body": "Clients who find black too harsh, lighter natural lashes, and techs who want a soft brown hybrid or 'wispy natural' style on their menu. Brown also blends well as a highlight colour mixed into a black set."}, {"heading": "Which thickness for which set", "body": "Use 0.10mm for classic one-to-one brown sets, 0.07mm for 2D-4D fans and hybrids, and 0.05mm for fuller volume. Brown fibres look lighter on the eye, so many artists go one step fuller than they would in black."}, {"heading": "Ordering from Lashtribe Africa", "body": "Lashtribe Africa is a preorder wholesale shop for lash technicians in Kenya. Your order joins the next supplier shipping batch, which leaves around the middle and the end of every month, so you pay close to source prices instead of local shelf prices.\n\nBuy the minimum quantity shown on this page to get the wholesale price; smaller orders pay the retail price. Pay by M-Pesa or card. Shipping to our office is worked out by weight at checkout, and we contact you as soon as your batch lands to arrange delivery to your salon."}], "specs": [{"label": "Type", "value": "Brown individual lash extensions"}, {"label": "Thickness", "value": "0.05mm, 0.07mm, 0.10mm"}, {"label": "Curl", "value": "C, D"}, {"label": "Length", "value": "8mm to 15mm single lengths, plus mixed 8-15mm trays"}, {"label": "Fibre", "value": "PBT synthetic fibre from Korea"}, {"label": "Colour", "value": "Brown"}], "faqs": [{"q": "Where can I buy brown lash extensions in Kenya?", "a": "Order brown lash extensions here on Lashtribe Africa. Add it to your cart, pay by M-Pesa or card, and it ships with the next supplier batch to our office in Kenya. We contact you when it arrives to arrange delivery to your salon or home."}, {"q": "How much is a brown lash tray in Kenya?", "a": "The price on this page is the live price. Order the minimum quantity for the wholesale price; smaller orders pay the retail price. Shipping is added by weight at checkout, so you see the full cost before you pay."}, {"q": "Do brown lashes look natural on dark lashes?", "a": "They give a softer effect than black and can look natural on dark lashes, especially mixed into a hybrid. For a strong, defined look, stay with black."}, {"q": "Can I mix brown and black lashes?", "a": "Yes. A few brown lashes in a black set adds dimension without looking coloured."}]}$j$::jsonb, $j$Brown lash extensions tray with rows of brown lashes and a close-up of the brown fibres$j$),
  ($j$qeelasee-camellia-lash$j$, $j$Camellia lashes have three different lengths in each strip, such as 8, 10 and 12mm, so every fan you pick already has built-in texture. They are a quick way to make soft, fluffy, textured volume sets. Choose 0.03mm, 0.05mm or 0.07mm, J, C or D curl, and length groups from 6-8-10mm up to 14-16-18mm.$j$, $j$["3 mixed lengths in each strip", "0.03, 0.05 and 0.07mm", "J, C and D curl", "Length groups 6-8-10mm to 14-16-18mm"]$j$::jsonb, $j${"title": "Camellia Lashes, 3 Mixed Lengths per Strip | Kenya", "meta": "Camellia lashes with three mixed lengths in one strip for quick textured volume. 0.03-0.07mm, J, C or D curl. Wholesale camellia lashes in Kenya.", "keyword": "camellia lashes", "keywords": ["camellia lash extensions", "mixed length lash tray", "3 lengths in one lash strip", "volume lash Kenya", "easy volume lashes"], "alt": "Camellia lashes tray with mixed-length strips and an eye wearing a textured volume set", "sections": [{"heading": "Why camellia lashes", "body": "Because each strip mixes three lengths, the fans come out with uneven, natural-looking tips without you mixing lengths by hand. That saves time on textured volume and wispy sets."}, {"heading": "Choosing a length group", "body": "The group names the three lengths in each strip. Pick the group whose middle length matches the main length in your lash map, for example 10-12-14mm for a set mapped around 12mm."}, {"heading": "Ordering from Lashtribe Africa", "body": "Lashtribe Africa is a preorder wholesale shop for lash technicians in Kenya. Your order joins the next supplier shipping batch, which leaves around the middle and the end of every month, so you pay close to source prices instead of local shelf prices.\n\nBuy the minimum quantity shown on this page to get the wholesale price; smaller orders pay the retail price. Pay by M-Pesa or card. Shipping to our office is worked out by weight at checkout, and we contact you as soon as your batch lands to arrange delivery to your salon."}], "specs": [{"label": "Type", "value": "Camellia lash extensions, 3 lengths per strip"}, {"label": "Thickness", "value": "0.03mm, 0.05mm, 0.07mm"}, {"label": "Curl", "value": "J, C, D"}, {"label": "Length groups", "value": "6-8-10mm, 7-9-11mm, 8-10-12mm, 9-11-13mm, 10-12-14mm, 11-13-15mm, 12-14-16mm, 13-15-17mm, 14-16-18mm"}, {"label": "Fibre", "value": "PBT synthetic fibre from Korea"}, {"label": "Colour", "value": "Black"}], "faqs": [{"q": "Where can I buy camellia lashes in Kenya?", "a": "Order camellia lashes here on Lashtribe Africa. Add it to your cart, pay by M-Pesa or card, and it ships with the next supplier batch to our office in Kenya. We contact you when it arrives to arrange delivery to your salon or home."}, {"q": "How much are camellia lashes in Kenya?", "a": "The price on this page is the live price. Order the minimum quantity for the wholesale price; smaller orders pay the retail price. Shipping is added by weight at checkout, so you see the full cost before you pay."}, {"q": "Do I fan camellia lashes myself?", "a": "Yes, pick and fan them like normal volume lashes. The mixed lengths give the texture."}, {"q": "Which thickness is best?", "a": "0.07mm for 2D-4D, 0.05mm for 4D-6D and 0.03mm for fuller fans."}]}$j$::jsonb, $j$Camellia lashes tray with mixed-length strips and an eye wearing a textured volume set$j$),
  ($j$qeelasee-classic-lash$j$, $j$These classic lash extension trays are for one-to-one sets, where you bond one extension to each natural lash. Choose from five thicknesses (0.10mm to 0.20mm), six curls from J to DD, and single lengths from 6mm to 20mm or a mixed 8-15mm tray. The fibres are soft matte PBT, so a full classic set looks clean and defined without feeling heavy.$j$, $j$["0.10-0.20mm thickness for one-to-one sets", "J, B, C, CC, D and DD curls", "6-20mm single lengths or mixed 8-15mm tray", "Soft matte PBT fibre"]$j$::jsonb, $j${"title": "Classic Lash Extensions Trays 0.10-0.20mm | Kenya", "meta": "Classic lash extension trays in 0.10-0.20mm, J to DD curls and 6-20mm lengths for one-to-one sets. Wholesale prices for lash techs in Kenya.", "keyword": "classic lash extensions", "keywords": ["classic eyelash extensions Kenya", "individual lash extensions", "classic lash trays", "lash extension trays Nairobi", "0.15 classic lashes", "eyelash extension supplies Kenya"], "alt": "Classic lash extensions tray with black lashes in rows and a close-up of the finished classic set", "sections": [{"heading": "What classic lashes are for", "body": "Classic lashes are the base of every lash menu: one extension on one natural lash. They give a mascara look that suits first-time clients, office looks and anyone who wants definition rather than volume.\n\nThe 0.15mm thickness is the usual starting point. Go down to 0.10mm or 0.12mm for fine or weak natural lashes, and use 0.18mm or 0.20mm only on strong, healthy lashes."}, {"heading": "Choosing curl, thickness and length", "body": "J and B curls give the softest, most natural lift. C is the everyday curl most clients ask for, CC adds a little more lift, and D and DD give an open, dramatic look. Match the thickness to the health of the natural lash: thinner fibres are lighter on weak lashes, thicker fibres suit strong ones. Pick lengths by mapping the eye first, then keep a mixed tray at your station for quick fills."}, {