  ($j$qeelasee-ellipse-flat-lash-black$j$, $j$Ellipse flat lash extensions are pressed flat at the base with split tips, so a 0.15mm or 0.20mm flat lash looks as dark and full as a thick classic lash but weighs less. The flat base also gives more contact with the natural lash for good retention. This black tray comes in 0.15mm, 0.20mm and 0.25mm, curls J to DD, 8-18mm.$j$, $j$["Black ellipse flat lashes with split tips", "Fuller look, lighter weight", "0.15, 0.20 and 0.25mm", "J to DD curls, 8-18mm"]$j$::jsonb, $j${"title": "Ellipse Flat Lash Extensions Black 0.15-0.25mm | Kenya", "meta": "Black ellipse flat lash extensions with split tips: the look of a thick classic lash at a lighter weight. 0.15-0.25mm, J to DD. Wholesale in Kenya.", "keyword": "ellipse flat lash extensions", "keywords": ["flat lashes Kenya", "ellipse lashes", "split tip flat lashes", "cashmere flat lashes", "classic flat lash trays"], "alt": "Black ellipse flat lash extensions tray with a close-up of the flattened split-tip lash", "sections": [{"heading": "Why flat lashes", "body": "A round classic lash gets heavier as it gets thicker. An ellipse lash is flattened, so you get the dark, bold line of a thick lash with less weight on the natural lash. The split tip makes the end look soft and feathery rather than blunt."}, {"heading": "Who it suits", "body": "Classic artists who want a fuller, darker classic set, clients with healthy lashes who want definition, and techs who want a quicker 'bold classic' service."}, {"heading": "Which thickness", "body": "0.15mm flat gives roughly the look of a 0.20mm round lash. Use 0.20mm and 0.25mm flat for strong lashes and bold sets only."}, {"heading": "Ordering from Lashtribe Africa", "body": "Lashtribe Africa is a preorder wholesale shop for lash technicians in Kenya. Your order joins the next supplier shipping batch, which leaves around the middle and the end of every month, so you pay close to source prices instead of local shelf prices.\n\nBuy the minimum quantity shown on this page to get the wholesale price; smaller orders pay the retail price. Pay by M-Pesa or card. Shipping to our office is worked out by weight at checkout, and we contact you as soon as your batch lands to arrange delivery to your salon."}], "specs": [{"label": "Type", "value": "Ellipse (flat) lash extensions, split tips"}, {"label": "Thickness", "value": "0.15mm, 0.20mm, 0.25mm"}, {"label": "Curl", "value": "J, B, C, CC, D, DD"}, {"label": "Length", "value": "8mm to 18mm single lengths, plus mixed 8-15mm trays"}, {"label": "Fibre", "value": "PBT synthetic fibre from Korea, matte"}, {"label": "Colour", "value": "Black"}], "faqs": [{"q": "Where can I buy ellipse flat lash extensions in Kenya?", "a": "Order ellipse flat lash extensions here on Lashtribe Africa. Add it to your cart, pay by M-Pesa or card, and it ships with the next supplier batch to our office in Kenya. We contact you when it arrives to arrange delivery to your salon or home."}, {"q": "How much is an ellipse flat lash tray in Kenya?", "a": "The price on this page is the live price. Order the minimum quantity for the wholesale price; smaller orders pay the retail price. Shipping is added by weight at checkout, so you see the full cost before you pay."}, {"q": "Are flat lashes better than classic lashes?", "a": "They look fuller for the same weight and have more surface to bond, which helps retention. Many artists use them for classic sets."}, {"q": "Can I use flat lashes on weak natural lashes?", "a": "Use the thinnest option (0.15mm) and shorter lengths on weak lashes, or choose a fine classic lash instead."}]}$j$::jsonb, $j$Black ellipse flat lash extensions tray with a close-up of the flattened split-tip lash$j$),
  ($j$qeelasee-ellipse-flat-lash-brown$j$, $j$Brown flat lash extensions (ellipse lashes) are pressed flat at the base with split tips, so a 0.15mm or 0.20mm flat lash looks as dark and full as a thick classic lash but weighs less. The flat base also gives more contact with the natural lash for good retention. This brown tray comes in 0.15mm, 0.20mm and 0.25mm, curls J to DD, 8-18mm.$j$, $j$["Brown ellipse flat lashes with split tips", "Fuller look, lighter weight", "0.15, 0.20 and 0.25mm", "J to DD curls, 8-18mm"]$j$::jsonb, $j${"title": "Ellipse Flat Lash Extensions Brown 0.15-0.25mm | Kenya", "meta": "Brown flat lash extensions (ellipse) with split tips: the look of a thick classic lash at a lighter weight. 0.15-0.25mm, J to DD. Wholesale in Kenya.", "keyword": "brown flat lash extensions", "keywords": ["flat lashes Kenya", "ellipse lashes", "split tip flat lashes", "cashmere flat lashes", "classic flat lash trays", "brown flat lashes"], "alt": "Brown ellipse flat lash extensions tray with a close-up of the flattened split-tip lash", "sections": [{"heading": "Why flat lashes", "body": "A round classic lash gets heavier as it gets thicker. An ellipse lash is flattened, so you get the dark, bold line of a thick lash with less weight on the natural lash. The split tip makes the end look soft and feathery rather than blunt."}, {"heading": "Who it suits", "body": "Classic artists who want a fuller, darker classic set, clients with healthy lashes who want definition, and techs who want a quicker 'bold classic' service. Brown flat lashes give the same effect with a softer colour for lighter lashes and natural looks."}, {"heading": "Which thickness", "body": "0.15mm flat gives roughly the look of a 0.20mm round lash. Use 0.20mm and 0.25mm flat for strong lashes and bold sets only."}, {"heading": "Ordering from Lashtribe Africa", "body": "Lashtribe Africa is a preorder wholesale shop for lash technicians in Kenya. Your order joins the next supplier shipping batch, which l