  ($j$qeelasee-l-curl-lash$j$, $j$L curl lash extensions have a flat base and then lift sharply, so they sit along a straight or downward-pointing natural lash and open the eye like a lash lift. Choose thickness from 0.05mm for volume up to 0.20mm for classic sets. Curls come in L, L+, LC and LD, in lengths from 8mm to 18mm or a mixed tray.$j$, $j$["0.05-0.20mm for volume and classic", "L, L+, LC and LD curls", "Ideal for hooded and straight lashes", "8-18mm lengths or mixed tray"]$j$::jsonb, $j${"title": "L Curl Lash Extensions L, L+, LC, LD | Kenya", "meta": "L curl lash extensions in L, L+, LC and LD for hooded, straight or downward lashes. 0.05-0.20mm, 8-18mm lengths. Wholesale in Kenya.", "keyword": "L curl lash extensions", "keywords": ["L curl lashes Kenya", "LC LD curl lashes", "lash extensions for hooded eyes", "L+ curl lashes", "lash lift effect extensions"], "alt": "L Curl Lash tray with black L shaped lash extensions and a close-up of the L curl bend", "sections": [{"heading": "Why L curls", "body": "Many clients have straight or downward-growing natural lashes, or hooded and monolid eyes where a C or D curl disappears under the lid. The flat base of an L curl bonds along more of the natural lash and then turns up, so the set stays visible and lifts the eye."}, {"heading": "L, L+, LC or LD?", "body": "L has the straightest base and a sharp lift. L+ lifts a little more. LC and LD have a softer, rounder L shape that blends with C and D curl sets, so they are useful on the inner and outer corners."}, {"heading": "Application tips", "body": "Place the extension along the natural lash with the bend just past the end of the natural lash's straight section. Check from the side so the lift points the same way across the set."}, {"heading": "Ordering from Lashtribe Africa", "body": "Lashtribe Africa is a preorder wholesale shop for lash technicians in Kenya. Your order joins the next supplier shipping batch, which leaves around the middle and the end of every month, so you pay close to source prices instead of local shelf prices.\n\nBuy the minimum quantity shown on this page to get the wholesale price; smaller orders pay the retail price. Pay by M-Pesa or card. Shipping to our office is worked out by weight at checkout, and we contact you as soon as your batch lands to arrange delivery to your salon."}], "specs": [{"label": "Type", "value": "L curl lash extensions"}, {"label": "Thickness", "value": "0.05mm, 0.07mm, 0.10mm, 0.12mm, 0.15mm, 0.18mm, 0.20mm"}, {"label": "Curl", "value": "L, LC, LD, L+"}, {"label": "Length", "value": "8mm to 18mm single lengths, plus mixed 8-15mm trays"}, {"label": "Fibre", "value": "PBT synthetic fibre from Korea"}, {"label": "Colour", "value": "Black"}], "faqs": [{"q": "Where can I buy L curl lash extensions in Kenya?", "a": "Order L curl lash extensions here on Lashtribe Africa. Add it to your cart, pay by M-Pesa or card, and it ships with the next supplier batch to our office in Kenya. We contact you when it arrives to arrange delivery to your salon or home."}, {"q": "How much is an L curl lash tray in Kenya?", "a": "The price on this page is the live price. Order the minimum quantity for the wholesale price; smaller orders pay the retail price. Shipping is added by weight at checkout, so you see the full cost before you pay."}, {"q": "Are L curl lashes good for hooded eyes?", "a": "Yes. The flat base and sharp lift keep the extensions visible above a hooded lid, which a normal curl often cannot do."}, {"q": "Can I mix L curls with C or D curls?", "a": "Yes. LC and LD blend especially well with C and D curls in the same set."}]}$j$::jsonb, $j$L Curl Lash tray with black L shaped lash extensions and a close-up of the L curl bend$j$),
