  ($j$lash-glue-10ml$j$, $j$A professional 10ml lash glue for eyelash extensions, supplied in a black bottle inside a resealable black pouch that keeps out light and moisture. Use it for classic, hybrid and volume sets.$j$, $j$["Professional lash extension glue", "10ml bottle", "Comes in a resealable pouch"]$j$::jsonb, $j${"title": "Lash Glue 10ml for Eyelash Extensions | Kenya", "meta": "Professional 10ml lash glue for eyelash extensions, in a sealed black bottle and pouch. Order lash glue at wholesale prices in Kenya.", "keyword": "lash glue 10ml", "keywords": ["eyelash extension glue", "black lash glue", "professional lash adhesive", "lash glue Nairobi", "lash glue Kenya", "eyelash extension glue price in Kenya"], "alt": "Lash glue 10ml black bottle with silver cap beside a black resealable pouch", "sections": [{"heading": "Who it suits", "body": "Lash techs who want a dependable everyday glue."}, {"heading": "Choosing a drying speed", "body": "The faster a glue dries, the less time you have to place and adjust each lash, so very fast glues suit experienced volume artists and slower glues suit beginners and classic work. Humidity changes drying speed too: lash glue sets faster in humid air and slower in dry air, which is why many artists in Nairobi keep two glues for the dry and rainy seasons."}, {"heading": "Storing your glue", "body": "Keep the bottle tightly closed in a cool, dry place; the supplier recommends 3-7°C, such as a fridge, for unopened bottles. Take it out about 20 minutes before use so it reaches room temperature, shake well, and wipe the nozzle clean before closing. Unopened glue keeps about a year; once opened, use it within 1-3 months for the best bond."}, {"heading": "Ordering from Lashtribe Africa", "body": "Lashtribe Africa is a preorder wholesale shop for lash technicians in Kenya. Your order joins the next supplier shipping batch, which leaves around the middle and the end of every month, so you pay close to source prices instead of local 