  ($j$qeelasee-m-curl-lash$j$, $j$M curl lash extensions have a longer flat base than an L curl and then a softer lift. They lie along straight, downward or short natural lashes and lift the tips into view, which makes them a favourite for monolid and hooded eyes. The supplier offers 0.03mm, 0.07mm and 0.10mm in a mixed 8-15mm tray.$j$, $j$["Long flat base, soft lift", "For monolid, hooded and straight lashes", "0.03, 0.07 and 0.10mm from the supplier", "Mixed 8-15mm tray"]$j$::jsonb, $j${"title": "M Curl Lash Extensions for Hooded Eyes | Kenya", "meta": "M curl lash extensions for monolid, hooded and straight lashes: long flat base with a soft upward lift. Wholesale M curl lash trays in Kenya.", "keyword": "M curl lash extensions", "keywords": ["M curl lashes Kenya", "lash extensions for monolid eyes", "asian eye lash extensions", "hooded eye lashes", "straight lash extensions"], "alt": "M Curl Lash tray with black M shaped lash extensions and a close-up of the M curl base", "sections": [{"heading": "Why M curls", "body": "On a straight or downward natural lash, a regular C or D curl bonds at an angle and can point down or stick out. The long flat base of an M curl sits flush along the natural lash and then lifts, so retention is better and the lashes open the eye."}, {"heading": "M or L curl?", "body": "An L curl turns up sharply. An M curl has a longer base and a gentler lift. Choose M for very straight, short or downward lashes, and L when you want a stronger lift."}, {"heading": "Ordering from Lashtribe Africa", "body": "Lashtribe Africa is a preorder wholesale shop for lash technicians in Kenya. Your order joins the next supplier shipping batch, which leaves around the middle and the end of every month, so you pay close to source prices instead of local shelf prices.\n\nBuy the minimum quantity shown on this page to get the wholesale price; smaller orders pay the retail price. Pay by M-Pesa or card. Shipping to our office is worked out by weight at checkout, and we contact you as soon as your batch lands to arrange delivery to your salon."}], "specs": [{"label": "Type", "value": "M curl lash extensions"}, {"label": "Thickness", "value": "0.03mm, 0.07mm or 0.10mm (supplier listing)"}, {"label": "Curl", "value": "M"}, {"label": "Length", "value": "Mixed 8-15mm tray (supplier listing)"}, {"label": "Fibre", "value": "PBT synthetic fibre from Korea"}, {"label": "Colour", "value": "Black"}], "faqs": [{"q": "Where can I buy M curl lash extensions in Kenya?", "a": "Order M curl lash extensions here on Lashtribe Africa. Add it to your cart, pay by M-Pesa or card, and it ships with the next supplier batch to our office in Kenya. We contact you when it arrives to arrange delivery to your salon or home."}, {"q": "How much is an M curl lash tray in Kenya?", "a": "The price on this page is the live price. Order the minimum quantity for the wholesale price; smaller orders pay the retail price. Shipping is added by weight at checkout, so you see the full cost before you pay."}, {"q": "Are M curl lashes good for Asian or monolid eyes?", "a": "Yes, M curls were made for straight and downward lashes on monolid and hooded eyes."}, {"q": "What lengths do M curl trays come in?", "a": "The supplier sells M curl as a mixed 8-15mm tray."}]}$j$::jsonb, $j$M Curl Lash tray with black M shaped lash extensions and a close-up of the M curl base$j$),
