  ($j$qeelasee-remover-brush-pen$j$, $j$A lash remover in a pen with a brush tip. Twist the end and the thick remover comes onto the brush, ready to paint on the bond. Because the texture is thick, it does not flow into the eyes easily, and it works in about a minute. The supplier says the 5ml pen does 10-15 clients and the 10ml about 30, and both can be refilled.$j$, $j$["Brush-tip pen, twist to dispense", "Thick texture, less running", "Works in about 1 minute", "5ml or 10ml, refillable"]$j$::jsonb, $j${"title": "Lash Remover Brush Pen 5ml / 10ml | Kenya", "meta": "Lash remover brush pen: thick formula that does not run, twist-and-brush application, about 1 minute to work. 5ml or 10ml, refillable. Kenya.", "keyword": "lash remover pen", "keywords": ["remover brush pen", "eyelash extension remover Kenya", "lash glue remover pen", "refillable lash remover"], "alt": "Remover brush pen for lash extensions with its boxes and a brush applying remover to lashes", "sections": [{"heading": "How to use", "body": "Twist the end until remover reaches the brush, paint it on the extensions you want to remove and wait about one minute. Slide the extensions off, wipe away any residue with a paper towel or cotton pad and cleanse the lashes. Clean the pen tip with disinfectant and replace the cap."}, {"heading": "Safe removal, step by step", "body": "Protect the lower lashes with an under-eye pad and tape. Apply the remover to the bond area only, never near the waterline, and wait the time given. Slide the extensions off with a micro brush or tweezers without pulling, then cleanse the lashes with lash shampoo or a cleanser to take away any remover left behind."}, {"heading": "Ordering from Lashtribe Africa", "body": "Lashtribe Africa is a preorder wholesale shop for lash technicians in Kenya. Your order joins the next supplier shipping batch, which leaves around the middle and the end of every month, so you pay close to source prices instead of local shelf prices.\n\nBuy the minimu