  ($j$qeelasee-strong-glue-0505$j$, $j$Strong Glue 0505 is a thicker (strong viscosity) lash glue with a 1 second drying time. The extra second gives you time to place and adjust each lash, which makes it a good glue for classic sets and for artists still building speed. The label rates retention at 6-8 weeks; the supplier text says 8-9.$j$, $j$["1s drying time", "Strong viscosity", "Classic sets and beginners", "6-9 weeks retention"]$j$::jsonb, $j${"title": "Strong Lash Glue 0505, 1s Dry, Thick | Kenya", "meta": "Strong viscosity lash glue 0505 with a 1 second dry: more working time, a firm hold, 6-9 weeks retention. Good for classic and beginners. Kenya.", "keyword": "strong lash glue", "keywords": ["1 second lash glue", "strong viscosity eyelash glue", "lash glue for beginners", "classic lash glue", "lash glue Kenya", "eyelash extension glue price in Kenya"], "alt": "Strong Glue 0505 eyelash glue bottle, 10ml, dry time 1s", "sections": [{"heading": "Who it suits", "body": "Beginners, classic artists and anyone who wants more working time per lash."}, {"heading": "Choosing a drying speed", "body": "The faster a glue dries, the less time you have to place and adjust each lash, so very fast glues suit experienced volume artists and slower glues suit beginners and classic work. Humidity changes drying speed too: lash glue sets faster in humid air and slower in dry air, which is why many artists in Nairobi keep two glues for the dry and rainy seasons."}, {"heading": "Storing your glue", "body": "Keep the bottle tightly closed in a cool, dry place; the supplier recommends 3-7°C, such as a fridge, for unopened bottles. Take it out about 20 minutes before use so it reaches room temperature, shake well, and wipe the nozzle clean before closing. Unopened glue keeps about a year; once opened, use it within 1-3 months for the best bond."}, {"heading": "Ordering from Lashtribe Africa", "body": "Lashtribe Africa is a preorder wholesale shop for lash technicians in Kenya. Your 