  ($j$qeelasee-ultra-glue-0506$j$, $j$Ultra Glue 0506 is a 1 second lash glue that the supplier describes as low irritation. The slower set gives you time to place each lash neatly, and it suits classic sets and newer artists. The label rates retention at 6-8 weeks; the supplier text says 8-9.$j$, $j$["1s drying time", "Low irritation (supplier)", "Classic and beginner sets", "6-9 weeks retention"]$j$::jsonb, $j${"title": "Ultra Lash Glue 0506, 1s Dry, Low Irritation | Kenya", "meta": "Ultra Glue 0506: a 1 second, low irritation lash glue with 6-9 weeks retention. More working time for classic and beginner sets. Lash glue Kenya.", "keyword": "low irritation lash glue", "keywords": ["1 second lash glue", "ultra lash glue", "low fume eyelash glue", "lash glue for beginners", "lash glue Kenya", "eyelash extension glue price in Kenya"], "alt": "Ultra Glue 0506 eyelash glue bottle, 10ml, dry time 1s", "sections": [{"heading": "Who it suits", "body": "Classic artists, beginners and artists working on clients who find faster glues uncomfortable. Low irritation does not mean irritation free: still patch test."}, {"heading": "Choosing a drying speed", "body": "The faster a glue dries, the less time you have to place and adjust each lash, so very fast glues suit experienced volume artists and slower glues suit beginners and classic work. Humidity changes drying speed too: lash glue sets faster in humid air and slower in dry air, which is why many artists in Nairobi keep two glues for the dry and rainy seasons."}, {"heading": "Storing your glue", "body": "Keep the bottle tightly closed in a cool, dry place; the supplier recommends 3-7°C, such as a fridge, for unopened bottles. Take it out about 20 minutes before use so it reaches room temperature, shake well, and wipe the nozzle clean before closing. Unopened glue keeps about a year; once opened, use it within 1-3 months for the best bond."}, {"heading": "Ordering from Lashtribe Africa", "body": "Lashtribe Africa is a preorder