  ($j$qeelasee-volume-lash-0-02-0-03mm$j$, $j$Ultra-fine 0.02mm and 0.03mm lashes for mega volume. Because each fibre is so light, you can build dense handmade fans of eight lashes or more and still keep the weight on the natural lash low. Choose curls from J to DD and lengths from 6mm to 20mm, or a mixed 8-15mm tray.$j$, $j$["Ultra-fine 0.02mm and 0.03mm", "For dense mega volume fans", "J, B, C, CC, D and DD curls", "6-20mm single lengths or mixed 8-15mm"]$j$::jsonb, $j${"title": "Mega Volume Lashes 0.02 / 0.03mm Trays | Kenya", "meta": "Ultra-fine 0.02mm and 0.03mm mega volume lash trays for 8D-16D handmade fans. J to DD curls, 6-20mm. Wholesale lash supplies in Kenya.", "keyword": "mega volume lashes", "keywords": ["0.03 volume lashes", "0.02 lashes", "mega volume lash trays Kenya", "ultra fine volume lashes", "russian volume lash extensions", "lash supplies Nairobi"], "alt": "Mega volume lash tray with ultra-fine 0.02/0.03mm black lashes and a handmade fan picked up from a fingertip", "sections": [{"heading": "Who it suits", "body": "Experienced volume and mega volume artists, and anyone doing dramatic, dark, fluffy sets for events and photos. If you are still learning to fan, start with 0.05mm or 0.07mm, as 0.02-0.03mm lashes are very fine and take practice to pick up evenly."}, {"heading": "Working with ultra-fine lashes", "body": "Use a light hand and fine-tipped volume tweezers, keep the room humidity steady and use a fast-drying glue with a thin, quick dip so the fan does not close up. Peel from the bottom row and keep the lid closed between picks so the fibres do not attract dust."}, {"heading": "Choosing curl, thickness and length", "body": "J and B curls give the softest, most natural lift. C is the everyday curl most clients ask for, CC adds a little more lift, and D and DD give an open, dramatic look. Match the thickness to the health of the natural lash: thinner fibres are lighter on weak lashes, thicker fibres suit strong ones. Pick lengths by mapping the eye first, then keep a mixed tray at your station for quick fills."}, {"heading": "Ordering from Lashtribe Africa", "body": "Lashtribe Africa is a preorder wholesale shop for lash technicians in Kenya. Your order joins the next supplier shipping batch, which leaves around the middle and the end of every month, so you pay close to source prices instead of local shelf prices.\n\nBuy the minimum quantity shown on this page to get the wholesale price; smaller orders pay the retail price. Pay by M-Pesa or card. Shipping to our office is worked out by weight at checkout, and we contact you as soon as your batch lands to arrange delivery to your salon."}], "specs": [{"label": "Type", "value": "Mega volume lash extensions for handmade fans"}, {"label": "Thickness", "value": "0.02mm, 0.03mm"}, {"label": "Curl", "value": "J, B, C, CC, D, DD"}, {"label": "Length", "value": "6mm to 20mm single lengths, plus mixed 8-15mm trays"}, {"label": "Fibre", "value": "PBT synthetic fibre from Korea"}, {"label": "Colour", "value": "Black"}], "faqs": [{"q": "Where can I buy mega volume lashes in Kenya?", "a": "Order mega volume lashes here on Lashtribe Africa. Add it to your cart, pay by M-Pesa or card, and it ships with the next supplier batch to our office in Kenya. We contact you when it arrives to arrange delivery to your salon or home."}, {"q": "How much is a 0.03 volume lash tray in Kenya?", "a": "The price on this page is the live price. Order the minimum quantity for the wholesale price; smaller orders pay the retail price. Shipping is added by weight at checkout, so you see the full cost before you pay."}, {"q": "How many lashes per fan with 0.03mm?", "a": "Fans of six to ten 0.03mm lashes, or more with 0.02mm, are common in mega volume. Always judge by the strength of the natural lash."}, {"q": "Do I need special glue?", "a": "A fast-drying volume glue (around 0.5s or quicker) helps hold wide fans. See our volume glues."}]}$j$::jsonb, $j$Mega volume lash tray with ultra-fine 0.02/0.03mm black lashes and a handmade fan picked up from a fingertip$j$),
  ($j$qeelasee-volume-lash-0-05-0-07mm$j$, $j$These are 0.05mm and 0.07mm volume lash extension trays for building your own handmade fans. 0.07mm is the go-to for 2D to 4D fans and hybrid sets, and 0.05mm lets you go fuller, around 4D to 6D, while keeping the weight safe for the natural lash. Six curls from J to DD and lengths from 6mm to 20mm cover full sets and fills.$j$, $j$["0.05mm and 0.07mm thickness", "For handmade 2D-6D fans and hybrids", "J, B, C, CC, D and DD curls", "6-20mm single lengths or mixed 8-15mm"]$j$::jsonb, $j${"title": "Volume Lash Extensions 0.05 / 0.07mm Trays | Kenya", "meta": "Volume lash extensions in 0.05mm and 0.07mm for handmade fans and hybrid sets. J to DD curls, 6-20mm lengths. Wholesale volume lashes in Kenya.", "keyword": "volume lash extensions", "keywords": ["0.07 volume lashes", "0.05 volume lashes", "volume lash trays Kenya", "russian volume lashes", "hybrid lash extensions", "lash extension supplies Kenya"], "alt": "Volume lash extensions tray in 0.05/0.07mm with black lashes and an inset eye wearing a full volume set", "sections": [{"heading": "Which thickness to pick", "body": "0.07mm is the most used volume thickness: easy to fan, and dark enough for a hybrid set when mixed with classics. 0.05mm is softer and lighter, so you can add more lashes per fan for a fuller look without overloading the natural lash.\n\nAs a rule, the more lashes in a fan, the finer each lash should be."}, {"heading": "Making fans from the tray", "body": "Peel a strip from the bottom row, lay it on your lash tile or tape and pick up two to six lashes with volume tweezers. Wiggle or roll them open into a fan, close the base in a thin layer of glue and place it on one natural lash."}, {"heading": "Choosing curl, thickness and length", "body": "J and B curls give the softest, most natural lift. C is the everyday curl most clients ask for, CC adds a little more lift, and D and DD give an open, dramatic look. Match the thickness to the health of the natural lash: thinner fibres are lighter on weak lashes, thicker fibres suit strong ones. Pick lengths by mapping the eye first, then keep a mixed tray at your station for quick fills."}, {"heading": "Ordering from Lashtribe Africa", "body": "Lashtribe Africa is a preorder wholesale shop for lash technicians in Kenya. Your order joins the next supplier shipping batch, which leaves around the middle and the end of every month, so you pay close to source prices instead of local shelf prices.\n\nBuy the minimum quantity shown on this page to get the wholesale price; smaller orders pay the retail price. Pay by M-Pesa or card. Shipping to our office is worked out by weight at checkout, and we contact you as soon as your batch lands to arrange delivery to your salon."}], "specs": [{"label": "Type", "value": "Volume lash extensions for handmade fans"}, {"label": "Thickness", "value": "0.05mm, 0.07mm"}, {"label": "Curl", "value": "J, B, C, CC, D, DD"}, {"label": "Length", "value": "6mm to 20mm single lengths, plus mixed 8-15mm trays"}, {"label": "Fibre", "value": "PBT synthetic fibre from Korea"}, {"label": "Colour", "value": "Black"}], "faqs": [{"q": "Where can I buy volume lash extensions in Kenya?", "a": "Order volume lash extensions here on Lashtribe Africa. Add it to your cart, pay by M-Pesa or card, and it ships with the next supplier batch to our office in Kenya. We contact you when it arrives to arrange delivery to your salon or home."}, {"q": "How much is a volume lash tray in Kenya?", "a": "The price on this page is the live price. Order the minimum quantity for the wholesale price; smaller orders pay the retail price. Shipping is added by weight at checkout, so you see the full cost before you pay."}, {"q": "Is 0.07 or 0.05 better for volume lashes?", "a": "0.07mm suits 2D-4D fans and hybrids; 0.05mm suits fuller 4D-6D fans. Many techs keep both and choose by the client's natural lashes."}, {"q": "Can beginners use these?", "a": "Yes, but if you are still learning to fan, our easy fan or premade fan trays are quicker while you practise."}]}$j$::jsonb, $j$Volume lash extensions tray in 0.05/0.07mm with black lashes and an inset eye wearing a full volume set$j$),
  ($j$qeelasee-w-shape-lash-6d-black$j$, $j$W shape lashes are ready-made fans where 6 lash fibres are joined at one base and open into a W, so each pick gives an even 6D fan with no hand fanning. These black 6D W lashes are 0.07mm, in C or D curl, with single lengths from 8mm to 15mm or a mixed tray. They are a quick way to do fluffy, textured volume and the popular "W lash" sets.$j$, $j$["6 fibres per fan, W shape", "0.07mm, C and D curl", "8-15mm single lengths or mixed tray", "Black colour"]$j$::jsonb, $j${"title": "6D W Shape Lash Extensions Black 0.07mm | Kenya", "meta": "Black 6D W shape lashes: 6 fibres joined at the base into a ready-made fan. 0.07mm, C or D curl, 8-15mm. Wholesale in Kenya.", "keyword": "6D W lashes", "keywords": ["6D premade fans", "W shape lash extensions Kenya", "6D lashes Kenya", "premade volume lashes", "W lashes"], "alt": "Black 6D W shape lash extensions tray with a close-up of a 6-fibre W fan", "sections": [{"heading": "Why W shape lashes", "body": "The fibres are joined in production, so every fan is the same width and the base is thin and clean. You pick, dip and place, which makes a full 6D set much quicker than hand-made fans and easy to repeat client after client."}, {"heading": "Who it suits", "body": "Salons that want fast, consistent volume, newer artists offering volume before they can hand-fan, and anyone doing the trendy wispy W lash look."}, {"heading": "Application tips", "body": "Pick the fan by its base, dip only the base in glue, and place it on one isolated natural lash. Check the fan opens flat and points the same way as its neighbours."}, {"heading": "Ordering from Lashtribe Africa", "body": "Lashtribe Africa is a preorder wholesale shop for lash technicians in Kenya. Your order joins the next supplier shipping batch, which leaves around the middle and the end of every month, so you pay close to source prices instead of local shelf prices.\n\nBuy the minimum quantity shown on this page to get the wholesale price;